@page "/background-jobs"
@using Odyssey.Client.Pages.Finance.ExchangeRateSync
@attribute [Authorize(Policy = PermissionClaims.SystemSettingsRead)]

<PageTitle>Background jobs</PageTitle>

@*
    Background jobs — what the server runs on its own, and how each run went (Odyssey Design System ·
    ui_kits/web/BackgroundJobs.jsx; docs/components-exchange-rate-sync.md, "Background jobs"). Gated on
    system-settings.read, like the jobs' settings.

    One section per job, headed by its name. It starts with the exchange-rate sync's run history, moved
    here from Currencies as it was; a job added later gets its own section. A job's controls stay with
    what it works on: the sync's status, Run now and Refresh are on Currencies, whose header menu links
    here.

    The page's one action is the header menu's "Refresh runs": it re-reads every section's runs, each
    keeping its page, and announces it politely, so a Running row can be seen to finish without a reload.
    Nothing polls.
*@

<OdsLiveAnnouncer @ref="_announcer" />

<MudStack Spacing="6">
    <PageHeader Title="Background jobs" Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Update">
        <SubLine>What the server runs on its own, and how each run went</SubLine>
        <ActionMenu>
            <MudMenuItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Refresh" OnClick="RefreshAsync">Refresh runs</MudMenuItem>
        </ActionMenu>
    </PageHeader>

    <section class="bgj-section" aria-labelledby="bgj-xrs-h">
        <h2 class="bgj-h" id="bgj-xrs-h">Exchange-rate sync</h2>
        <ExchangeRateSyncRunHistory @ref="_exchangeRateSyncRuns" />
    </section>
</MudStack>

@code {
    private OdsLiveAnnouncer? _announcer;
    private ExchangeRateSyncRunHistory? _exchangeRateSyncRuns;

    // Every section's runs, each re-read on the page it shows.
    private async Task RefreshAsync()
    {
        if (_exchangeRateSyncRuns is not null)
            await _exchangeRateSyncRuns.ReloadAsync();
        if (_announcer is not null)
            await _announcer.Announce("Runs refreshed");
    }
}
